{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you","id":1506764,"title":"This already happened to you?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-28T10:43:47-07:00","id":1506764,"title":"This already happened to you?","content":"When my cortorie was exploring the basement of an abandoned house we found a wight inside that stirred when we met and he came at us, one of my &quot;partners&quot; shot my character in the leg leaving me there to die, I I didn't have vitae to recover enough so I couldn't do much, the ST still wanted to try to help me, but it wasn't enough. Has anything like this ever happened to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T11:01:42-07:00","id":1506767,"title":"","content":"it hasn't,personally even in a pvp game i'd ask permission before trying to hurt your character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T11:42:39-07:00","id":1506773,"title":"","content":"Ah the old adage of <i><b>&quot;you don't have to be able to outrun a dragon, just your slowest party member&quot;</b></i> comes to mind. Sadly, in TTRPGs we dabble in bad situations, criminal professions, and other unsafe aspects of existence. But we often forget about the survival of the fittest behavior that is required to not die in such settings.<br /> <br /> The betrayal does suck, but at the same time it is part and parcel for the hobby. Just give the player a knowing smile and say that you look forward to meeting their next few characters, short lived though they may be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T12:47:20-07:00","id":1506779,"title":"","content":"Having been on both ends of player betrayals (plenty of times), there's nothing more frustrating than losing a favorite character, but also nothing quite like it to spice up group dynamics. It can produce some fine drama for a chronicle and only becomes a problem if the players take it OOC. Which happens too much, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> The Vampire LARP group I played in was pretty much political pvp. After all, you play egocentric, power-hungry monsters in a society in which the ability to backstab somebody and get away with it is seen as an admirable trait. When characters got too cozy with each other, it took away a lot of the thrill and the game started to get boring.<br /> I took that mentality back to TTRPGs with me, and inter-group squabbles remain one of the most fun things for me, even when I'm STing.<br /> <br /> tldr: if all parties involved can accept it as part of the game, it's part of the fun; if someone can't, it needs to be discussed before it causes OOC drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T14:21:53-07:00","id":1506788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you#post1506764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When my cortorie was exploring the basement of an abandoned house we found a wight inside that stirred when we met and he came at us, one of my &quot;partners&quot; shot my character in the leg leaving me there to die, I I didn't have vitae to recover enough so I couldn't do much, the ST still wanted to try to help me, but it wasn't enough. Has anything like this ever happened to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say I've had this particular situation happen to me... mostly because backstabbing in this situation makes zero sense (if you're good enough with a gun to injure a vampire with one badly enough they can't flee a fight... you were good enough to shoot the wight's leg instead).<br /> <br /> I've been on the losing end of PC on PC betrayals before. I personally don't get the appeal when it gets to really high stakes stuff like character-death. I've never seen it actually be fun for everyone involved. Rivalries over Backgrounds, competing for favor from NPCs, who gets to Embrace a high value potential childe, jockeying for position within the coterie? Sure, bring all that stuff on. But vampires form coteries because there's strength in numbers - esp. for younger vampires aka the PCs - and it's in everyone's best interests not to take internal coterie bickering too far, or some more unified coterie will take advantage and take you all out. If the wider vampire community knows a wight can destroy the basic trust of mutual-self interest in your coterie, then your coterie is going to get torn apart so other people can have all your group's stuff.<br /> <br /> As PCs get more powerful (both with XP and more narrative things) and less dependent on their coterie for mutual protection from the greed of vampire society, the conflicts still tend to keep away from PC on PC killings, because they're going to be able to send proxies to fight proxies instead. You persisted that far by working on making sure you're not in a position to be killed off that readily by others.<br /> <br /> Of course tastes vary, and has been noted, this is really something groups need to discuss to keep things fun. Some people like really back-stab heavy games, and some people hate PvP play completely. Whatever is fun for the group is more important than appeals to how vampires &quot;should&quot; be played.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506773#post1506773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we often forget about the survival of the fittest behavior that is required to not die in such settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not what Survival of the Fittest means, or the &quot;Fittest&quot; part wouldn't be necessary. You need to not just survive, but survive long enough to hit benchmarks that demonstrate fitness. In biology where this comes from and all, fitness is generally measured by ensuring your genes are perpetuated in the population (which means applying the concept to most RPGs doesn't work because very few RPGs get into that). How many grandchildren an individual has that survive to reproductive age is a common metric of fitness for example.<br /> <br /> Betrayal is part of fitness in many social organisms, but it's a high risk strategy because if you're too blatant or too frequent with it, you get kicked out of the social group you're relying on for survival. Vampires engaging in prestation are going to want higher prices and more assurances from a vampire that's known for backstabbing their coterie because they're probably going to considering backstabbing favor-traders to avoid getting out of their debts too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The betrayal does suck, but at the same time it is part and parcel for the hobby. Just give the player a knowing smile and say that you look forward to meeting their next few characters, short lived though they may be. </div> </div> </div>Eh... I don't think that's a very good way to treat this. It's common in the hobby, but it's growing to be less so, and it's never an essential part of it. Making revenge PCs to backstab the PCs that backstabbed your old PC is OOC drama a lot of people want zero part in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T15:10:05-07:00","id":1506794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506788#post1506788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't say I've had this particular situation happen to me... mostly because backstabbing in this situation makes zero sense (if you're good enough with a gun to injure a vampire with one badly enough they can't flee a fight... you were good enough to shoot the wight's leg instead).<br /> <br /> I've been on the losing end of PC on PC betrayals before. I personally don't get the appeal when it gets to really high stakes stuff like character-death. I've never seen it actually be fun for everyone involved. Rivalries over Backgrounds, competing for favor from NPCs, who gets to Embrace a high value potential childe, jockeying for position within the coterie? Sure, bring all that stuff on. But vampires form coteries because there's strength in numbers - esp. for younger vampires aka the PCs - and it's in everyone's best interests not to take internal coterie bickering too far, or some more unified coterie will take advantage and take you all out. If the wider vampire community knows a wight can destroy the basic trust of mutual-self interest in your coterie, then your coterie is going to get torn apart so other people can have all your group's stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>He tried, but it was established that the wight in question was bulletproof, a nosferatu elder being more specific. According to the city court, they weren't happy, but they didn't punish them severely, as it was too much to ask for four neonates to handle one elder and also the situation ended up taking care of itself. (Long story)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T15:46:39-07:00","id":1506796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506788#post1506788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... I don't think that's a very good way to treat this. It's common in the hobby, but it's growing to be less so, and it's never an essential part of it. Making revenge PCs to backstab the PCs that backstabbed your old PC is OOC drama a lot of people want zero part in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it even common in the hobby anymore? I've had a feeling we've grown out of that juvenile phase.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T15:53:23-07:00","id":1506797,"title":"","content":"I've never had this happen to me, but issues about intra-party conflict affects a lot of RPG games. It is usually justified as &quot;I'm just playing my character&quot;, but if it is causing your fellow players to not have fun IRL it just destroys the gaming group. Players don't want other players crapping all over them and destroying their ability to enjoy the game. It's just not fun.<br /> <br /> And in my experience, the player who acts like a jerk and says &quot;I'm just playing my character&quot; tends to get really pissed off if NPCs or even other PCs react with outrage to their actions. Then getting another PC killed is just &quot;playing their character.&quot; Their PC getting killed in response becomes unacceptable (as is the idea that the other PCs won't accept the other PC into their group anymore and the ST telling that person he needs to create a new PC).<br /> <br /> Depending on the genre, what constitutes acceptable IC conflict can change. Players expect very little betrayal in heroic fantasy games, but expect some amount in a game like Vampire. In my gaming groups, players tend to be OK with a rare and skillful betrayal provided it allows them to continue playing their PC and the rationale for the coterie to continue exists. In very rare cases, the actual destruction of another PC may be acceptable, but the story behind that decision must be so good the other players are willing to accept this. But there is still a point when it crosses the line. Usually there is an unwritten agreement between members of the gaming table of what is acceptable or unacceptable. Sometimes that needs to be discussed or made explicit.<br /> <br /> Players having fun is an OCC issue. It is not an IC issue. You can never resolve these debates by handling them IC. The gaming group needs to determine what is acceptable behavior. IMO the excuse of &quot;I'm just roleplaying my character&quot; for ruining another player's fun means that player needs a new PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T15:58:48-07:00","id":1506798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506794#post1506794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He tried, but it was established that the wight in question was bulletproof, a nosferatu elder being more specific. According to the city court, they weren't happy, but they didn't punish them severely, as it was too much to ask for four neonates to handle one elder and also the situation ended up taking care of itself. (Long story)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that paints the other player in a better light, but your ST in a worse one... I'm not really sure what your ST was expecting to happen if the PCs are suddenly in a &quot;either some of us die, or all of us die,&quot; situation where a bunch of neonates are up against something tough enough that they don't really stand a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T16:46:29-07:00","id":1506803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506798#post1506798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that paints the other player in a better light, but your ST in a worse one... I'm not really sure what your ST was expecting to happen if the PCs are suddenly in a &quot;either some of us die, or all of us die,&quot; situation where a bunch of neonates are up against something tough enough that they don't really stand a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't judge him so seriously, it was normal for him to put up situations like that to see how we could get away, but to be honest I really don't think anyone expected what happened, apart from the fact that when it happened he was the only one who was upset with this attitude , the rest even laughed at the situation, he just didn't do anything more serious because I said I was fine with the result. He even let me play as a revenent after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T17:40:23-07:00","id":1506809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506788#post1506788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... not what Survival of the Fittest means, or the &quot;Fittest&quot; part wouldn't be necessary. You need to not just survive, but survive long enough to hit benchmarks that demonstrate fitness. In biology where this comes from and all, fitness is generally measured by ensuring your genes are perpetuated in the population (which means applying the concept to most RPGs doesn't work because very few RPGs get into that). How many grandchildren an individual has that survive to reproductive age is a common metric of fitness for example.<br /> <br /> Betrayal is part of fitness in many social organisms, but it's a high risk strategy because if you're too blatant or too frequent with it, you get kicked out of the social group you're relying on for survival. Vampires engaging in prestation are going to want higher prices and more assurances from a vampire that's known for backstabbing their coterie because they're probably going to considering backstabbing favor-traders to avoid getting out of their debts too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Survival of the fittest refers to both mental and physical strategies. As such you must be prepared for betrayal or at least vaguely aware of it to have any chance at avoiding it. It doesn't matter if you entering a room during a fire fight and making sure the person you don't trust is in front of you where you can keep your eyes on them or if you are wanting to get married to the love of your life, but still insist on a pre-nuptial agreement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506788#post1506788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... I don't think that's a very good way to treat this. It's common in the hobby, but it's growing to be less so, and it's never an essential part of it. Making revenge PCs to backstab the PCs that backstabbed your old PC is OOC drama a lot of people want zero part in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said to say it, I never said to do it, the standing threat is enough to correct future behavior in people who aren't complete jerks. Also if that player wasn't willing to deal with the fallout of pulling a stunt like that, then they shouldn't have done it. More importantly the ST screwed up here if this was going to be a problem. The wight didn't have to target the downed PC, it could just as easily think the PC was a snack for later that wasn't going anywhere and just gone after the other players.<br /> <br /> On a related note, the notion that the hobby has in some way matured is laughable. The game is as mature or immature as the Players using the rules. If you don't believe me, just check out the genre of D&amp;D horror stories on youtube or reddit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T19:34:49-07:00","id":1506815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506809#post1506809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Survival of the fittest refers to both mental and physical strategies.</div> </div> </div> </div>You quoted me saying that betrayal can be a fitness strategy. I'm not sure why you feel the need to state this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As such you must be prepared for betrayal or at least vaguely aware of it to have any chance at avoiding it. It doesn't matter if you entering a room during a fire fight and making sure the person you don't trust is in front of you where you can keep your eyes on them or if you are wanting to get married to the love of your life, but still insist on a pre-nuptial agreement. </div> </div> </div>None of this addressed what &quot;Survival of the Fittest&quot; actually means. These are just normal strategies for dealing with different types of betrayal that may or may not get into fitness. There is no correlation I'm aware of between pre-nups and biological fitness in humans, because fitness doesn't actually care if you get divorced and how resources are divided during divorce as long as you continue your genes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I said to say it, I never said to do it, the standing threat is enough to correct future behavior in people who aren't complete jerks. </div> </div> </div>If they're not complete jerks, you should be able to just talk to them without having to threaten them. IMO if you're threatening people in your gaming group over play, there are bigger problems than PCs betraying each other to deal with. Anyone that games with me and threatens people is on a fast track for getting kicked out of the group for being a jerk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More importantly the ST screwed up here if this was going to be a problem. </div> </div> </div>Did you read my previous post to this one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T20:06:11-07:00","id":1506818,"title":"","content":"Backtracking a bit, have I ever had a situation where my character got betrayed by another character, with possibly lethal consequences?<br /> <br /> Well, yeah, twice in fact, nearly three-but here's the thing, it was part of the group expectations when we made characters and gave the Storyteller ideas of how we wanted those games to run. One of them had it explicitly clear that the goal was for every character to have goals that they heavily prioritized, because that was a theme we all wanted to explore, just how much we were willing to sacrifice <i>for</i> those goals. I've had a lot more games where the group agreed at the start that, even if some inter-party conflict was fine, at the end of the day our characters were there for each other, and kept to it.<br /> <br /> RPG's, as a creative endeavor, are just as subject to the fact that they are games of setting and managing expectations, heavily weighted in a certain way because of the direct human interaction. It's important for enjoyment and exploration to make it clear what players are in for, what they're not in for, and checking for how those can change as the story progresses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T13:24:18-07:00","id":1506866,"title":"","content":"Never happened to my characters yet, but my Brujah character main job is getting the Baron out of harm's way and usually doesn't bother with wasteful conflict and my Malkavian and his buddies try to reduce risk as much as possible and use there auspex, celerity and obsfucate disciplines to get themselves out of trouble if there is a way out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T13:34:51-07:00","id":1506868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506815#post1506815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of this addressed what &quot;Survival of the Fittest&quot; actually means. These are just normal strategies for dealing with different types of betrayal that may or may not get into fitness. There is no correlation I'm aware of between pre-nups and biological fitness in humans, because fitness doesn't actually care if you get divorced and how resources are divided during divorce as long as you continue your genes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are too stupid to see the betrayal coming and take steps to protect yourself, you can't pass on your genes. Keeping with your limited view of what &quot;survival of the fittest&quot; means, if you lose most of your resources in a divorce, then your ability to procure another high quality mate decreases, which means even if you find another mate then they most likely will be of inferior quality, which means the offspring will be of likewise inferior quality, thus not the fittest.<br /> <br /> You are correct, nature does not care how you produce offspring, be it forming social bonds or using force to ensure offspring are produced. But the breeding stock that you choose is a concern. If they have diseases, bad genetics, or any number of other issues, then they might not be worth your time to attempt mating with. But since humans are social creatures, we create societies with artificial aspects that throw a curveball into what is an important trait or behavior. This means that behaviors or traits that would be a detriment in the wild are actually a boon in our artificial existence.<br /> <br /> A good example is the fact that in big business sociopathic tendencies are ten times more prevalent than in the general population. The lack of empathy and cutthroat behavior would get you exiled or ostracized from a tribe, but they tend to make you successful in business. This normally wouldn't be a problem, except that being successful in business means you attract a lot more potential breeding partners just due to the higher level of status and resources.<br /> <br /> But since we are talking about vampires, other than Clan &amp; Generation, there are no aspects of &quot;genes&quot; that really enter into the conversation. Instead &quot;Survival of the Fittest&quot; refers to a given vampires ability to be adaptable, to learn, to be cunning. In short to ensure their continued existence and defeat their opponents, or at least negate their enemies ability to do them harm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506815#post1506815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they're not complete jerks, you should be able to just talk to them without having to threaten them. IMO if you're threatening people in your gaming group over play, there are bigger problems than PCs betraying each other to deal with. Anyone that games with me and threatens people is on a fast track for getting kicked out of the group for being a jerk.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you run a game where the players can do this level of betrayal, things will go back and forth naturally. If you run a game where reprisals are not allowed, then you need to overide the betrayal so that it doesn't screw up the group.<br /> <br /> If you let the betrayal happen and then threaten the victim of the betrayal with exile when they promise to treat the betrayer in kind..... then you are the jerk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T14:27:04-07:00","id":1506872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506868#post1506868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are too stupid to see the betrayal coming and take steps to protect yourself, you can't pass on your genes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's entirely dependent on the circumstances of the betrayal in question. Which I acknowledged already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keeping with your limited view of what &quot;survival of the fittest&quot; means,... </div> </div> </div>No. Stop.<br /> <br /> I'm talking about survival of the fittest, a theory in the early conceptualization of evolution that's been heavily refined since but the original formulation is still useful enough in general conversation. You're talking about social Darwinism, which is pseudoscience nonsense that seeks to defined &quot;fitness&quot; in a fashion skewed by ideologies instead of actual study of human evolution. For example, you've directly correlated economic status with fitness, which has been repeatedly debunked. If humans solely selected for rich people, we'd only have rich people; which isn't actually possible. There is no way to objectively evaluate an individual as a &quot;high quality mate&quot; before hand;.it's always an attempt to make a best guess from microbes to humans. That's because, as I already noted, the metrics for fitness have to be measured in generational terms. Humans are especially difficult to assign any sort of &quot;high quality&quot; assessments to because we have invented so many different functional survival strategies for ourselves via our highly complex social structures. &quot;Wild&quot; vs. &quot;artificial&quot; is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This normally wouldn't be a problem, except that being successful in business means you attract a lot more potential breeding partners just due to the higher level of status and resources. </div> </div> </div>And when does this actually prove you're more biologically fit?<br /> <br /> Hint. It doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But since we are talking about vampires, other than Clan &amp; Generation, there are no aspects of &quot;genes&quot; that really enter into the conversation. </div> </div> </div>Which really means we're not talking about true survival of the fittest anyway, not that survival of the fittest gets a new definition. As I said before, survival of the fittest doesn't actually work when applied to RPGs, because few RPGs actually explore interactions in a context where it would matter. Vampires are just more on the nose about it because it's a defining aspect of VtM vampires, instead of just being a function of narrative conceit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In short to ensure their continued existence and defeat their opponents, or at least negate their enemies ability to do them harm. </div> </div> </div>Again, that's just survival. Calling it survival of the fittest is pointless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you run a game where the players can do this level of betrayal, things will go back and forth naturally. If you run a game where reprisals are not allowed, then you need to overide the betrayal so that it doesn't screw up the group.<br /> <br /> If you let the betrayal happen and then threaten the victim of the betrayal with exile when they promise to treat the betrayer in kind..... then you are the jerk. </div> </div> </div>You seem to be mixing up what's in-character and whats out-of-character. In-character betrayals can be answers with in-character reprisals. A player threatening reprisals, even in the form of new PCs that will kill the betrayer's PCs, is an out-of-character threat over in-character actions.<br /> <br /> You can't have a functional game where in-character betrayals are allowed, and let it spill over into out-of-character conflicts. I cannot comprehend the idea of the ST being a &quot;jerk&quot; if they stop in-character conflicts from spilling over into out-of-character drama. Who wants players threatening each other over a game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T03:13:19-07:00","id":1506935,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> do you even know what you are arguing about at this point?<br /> <br /> I disagree with your definition of survival of the fittest, which is a concept that predates most of the things you are attributing it to. End of discussion since you are not proving anything or citing sources.<br /> <br /> You admit that mental capacity is required to survive and be the fittest, but then in the same response you say that the intelligence required to be good at business isn't something to be considered for being biologically fit. Please pick a lane and stay in it.<br /> <br /> As for the how to handle group dynamics, I am not mixing up in and out of character stuff, because both are supposed to be agreed upon before the game starts. Like I said before, if your group agrees to run that sort of game, cool. If you want to run a game where that is forbidden, also cool. If you run a game where that comes out of nowhere and <i><b><u>isn't fun for everyone concerned</u></b></i>, to the point where you post on a forum about it, your game group is already screwed. The back and forth afterwards is more of a formality rather than something you can control by trying to social engineer the groups behavior after the fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T13:28:30-07:00","id":1506986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1506764-this-already-happened-to-you?p=1506935#post1506935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> do you even know what you are arguing about at this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'm arguing for:<br /> <br /> 1) The proper application of the concept of survival of the fittest<br /> <br /> 2) Not letting players threaten retaliation against other players over in-character actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree with your definition of survival of the fittest, which is a concept that predates most of the things you are attributing it to. </div> </div> </div>Herbert Spencer is credited with the phrase as a critique of Charles Darwin's choice of &quot;natural selection&quot; because Spencer disagreed with the anthropomorphic implications of nature picking winners and losers, instead of fitness being an emergent property. After some debate in the scientific community at the time, Darwin actually conceded the point and later editions of <i>On the Origin of Species </i>would have &quot;survival of the fittest&quot; added to them as a synonymous phrase for &quot;natural selection&quot; to help clarify that nature is not an active selective force even if it is easier to use that as a metaphor for people to understand the concepts at hand.<br /> <br /> What's your source for survival of the fittest predating this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You admit that mental capacity is required to survive and be the fittest, but then in the same response you say that the intelligence required to be good at business isn't something to be considered for being biologically fit. </div> </div> </div>No. I pointed out that there's no evidence for a correlation between sociopaths have success in business and them having increased biological fitness as you stated they would have. Power and prestige are certainly one method of attracting mates in human society, but it doesn't actually mean you end up with more kids than anyone else does, or that those kids will go one to have successful life strategies and have even more kids.<br /> <br /> Your problem here, is that like most people that end up talking about social Darwinism instead of survival of the fittest, is that you're putting the cart before the horse. Having good business sense is not, by itself, a sign of fitness in humans. Human mating is far more complex than that. Having good business sense can be part of a fitness strategy, but that needs to include a large number of unrelated traits to cover all the aspects of human pair-bonding and child rearing that don't follow the rules of businesses.<br /> <br /> As I said before, fitness in this sense has to be measured over generations and time. It's also something that needs to be analyzed at a population level, not just looking at specific individuals, because ultimately it's about what a population's traits look like over time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the how to handle group dynamics, I am not mixing up in and out of character stuff, because both are supposed to be agreed upon before the game starts. </div> </div> </div>You directly advocated for threatening the player of a character that betrayed your character with the promise of your future characters existing to ensure that player's characters are short lived.<br /> <br /> How is that not mixing in- and out-of-character stuff?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you run a game where that comes out of nowhere and <i><b><u>isn't fun for everyone concerned</u></b></i>, to the point where you post on a forum about it, your game group is already screwed. </div> </div> </div>Or not? The OP's group seems to be recovering from the incident without the game dissolving, and despite any tensions about what happened the group has, at least as reported, remained on good terms despite the OP coming here to asked the forums about their feelings on the matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The back and forth afterwards is more of a formality rather than something you can control by trying to social engineer the groups behavior after the fact. </div> </div> </div>I haven't had any issues controlling things by &quot;social engineering&quot; with simple rules like, &quot;if you have a problem with something another player had their character did to your character, we're going to talk about it respectfully, and if anyone starts verbally attacking or makes threats of in-game retaliation instead they're at risk of being booted from the game.&quot; I don't give a shit if it's a &quot;formality.&quot; It has no place in games I run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T10:24:39-07:00","id":1507191,"title":"","c